{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>A perpetual burnt offering for your generations.</b> After their entry into the land, for reason suggests that they did not offer a sacrifice except at Sinai alone — this is the עלת תמיד העשויה בהר סיני — and on the Day of Atonement in the second year, for it is written there ויעש כאשר צוה ה׳ את משה. And so the prophet said: הזבחים ומנחה הגשתם לי במדבר ארבעים שנה בית ישראל — for where did they have in the wilderness wine, oil, fine flour, and animals for the daily offerings every day, for the additional offerings, for Sabbaths, for new moons, and for the festivals, for all forty years? And one cannot answer from ואנחנו ובעירנו, for in that passage they were encamped at Kadesh and took plunder — animals — from the land of Midian, Sihon, and Og."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:08.936825587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}